This is a Jekyll + Minimal Mistakes blog, not a React/Tailwind app.

When changing UI:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/weo0o0-jekyll-ui/SKILL.md` and apply `impeccable`, `web-design-guidelines`, `frontend-design`, `check-fix-accessibility` as relevant.
2. Put new visual tokens in `assets/css/main.scss` (before theme `@import`) or `_sass/_weo0o0-overrides.scss`. Do not grow `_sass/minimal-mistakes/` with site-only CSS.
3. Keep Catppuccin Mocha surfaces (`#1e1e2e` base, `#cdd6f4` text) and brand teal `#00adb5`. Pair Gowun Batang (body) with Gowun Dodum (UI) and Pretendard fallback.
4. Preserve dark `color-scheme`, `:focus-visible`, and `prefers-reduced-motion` rules.
5. Verify with `npm run pa11y:home` / `npm run pa11y:ci` when a local Jekyll server is available.
